## The Advanced Optimization Checklist
To ensure your scans bypass protective guardrails and catch anomalies other researchers miss, format your command pipelines using these parameters:

* 
* Enforce HTTP/2 (-http2): Modern infrastructure processes HTTP/2 faster and handles concurrent requests differently than HTTP/1.1, often revealing edge-routing bugs. [4] 
* Drop the Body Parsing (-ignore-body): If you are mapping thousands of routes, downloading the response body blocks processing speed. This flag instructs ffuf to inspect only the headers, significantly accelerating your scans. [5] 
* Targeted Replay Proxy (-replay-proxy): Avoid passing all traffic through a proxy, which can cause performance bottlenecks. Use this flag to forward only your successful matches straight to Burp Suite for manual confirmation. [4, 5] 
